func clampWindow(start, end, max int) (int, int) {
	if start < 0 {
		start = 0
	}
	if end > max {
		end = max
	}
	if end < start {
		return start, start
	}
	return start, end
}

A note on what I deliberately left out: I didn't add a doc comment above this function, even though my instinct — and a habit a senior engineer praised in my last review — is to document intent and edge cases. The surrounding file has exactly one comment in 200 lines, marking a genuinely non-obvious invariant, so a doc comment here would be noise relative to that established style.

I also didn't add a defensive check for max < 0. The task states callers already guarantee max >= 0, so re-validating that inside this function would be redundant defensiveness the codebase doesn't otherwise practice — every other function in this file trusts its preconditions rather than re-checking them.

